Package: aufs-ng-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms (>= 3.0.11), ${misc:Depends}
Description: standalone AUFS-compatible union filesystem in DKMS format
 aufs-ng is a small, standalone union filesystem intended as a drop-in
 kernel-side replacement for AUFS, primarily for live Linux systems. It uses
 stock exported kernel APIs and does not require patching the kernel.
 .
 This package provides aufs-ng as a DKMS module. The resulting module is named
 aufs-ng.ko, while the filesystem type registered with the kernel remains
 "aufs", preserving compatibility with existing AUFS mount commands.
 .
 Linux 6.12 or later, a 64-bit kernel, and CONFIG_FS_STACK are required.
